    "overview": "The implemented world is the existing Hoard family: shared charcoal surfaces, Cinzel headings, Source Sans 3 controls and Daedalus's turquoise accent. Luis explicitly requested this family style and icon, superseding the earlier light inspection-bench direction. The north star below describes that implemented family workbench; it does not establish a new identity or an approved naming preference.\n\nA compact, flat workspace surrounds a distinct model field. Preparation, retained versions, optional print repair or game optimization, refinement or learned enlargement from an original 512 result to 1024, and export stay legible around the actual geometry. Equal comparison panes and linked orbit let the user inspect an original beside a later version; common clay material supports shape comparison, while color mode restores the available model color or materials.\n\nThis record follows the current client and the authentic desktop and mobile captures in `.impeccable/review/`, including the optional preparation controls. Construction was explicitly code-led: no approved visual comp, QUALITY BAR card or generated critique-reference exists, and no comp-fidelity claim is made. The captures show interface states, not evidence that pending CPU operations improved a model, verified closure or met a requested budget. The earlier FINISH-R3.md verdict remains limited to its original scope. The single earlier detector pass was DEGRADED and regex-only with parsers absent; neither context capture nor detector was repeated for this refresh. Those are evidence limits, not additional design rules.",
